    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c970266_87b78ceb",
        "filename": "common/charge_state_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1445,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-13T10:33:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern here that the charge_task in suspend (after a recent fix) only runs every minute.\nOne other way would be that if CMD_PWR is defined, then to reset the MAX_TIME to 500MS or so, and take the ~2mW hit that charge_task running that frequently does, and update the average that way. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "169273af_cbd211fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1445,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1445,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "5ea59932af2618665d724c566dd6abfb14b09b1c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "463f2ba4_c6595276",
        "filename": "common/charge_state_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1445,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-14T09:12:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be honest, you are likely to have a good chunk of the 2mW hit by running your own tick stuff.\nSo yes, you can just cap the sleep duration when the pwr measurement is *Enabled* (more than defined)\nif you can take advantage of the 1min average, this should be mostly solved though.",
      "parentUuid": "6c970266_87b78ceb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1445,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1445,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "5ea59932af2618665d724c566dd6abfb14b09b1c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bcd4fc42_6b2a75d5",
        "filename": "common/charge_state_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1453,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-13T10:07:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you don\u0027t need to do the division at every pass,\njust do it when the average is queried.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1453,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1453,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "5ea59932af2618665d724c566dd6abfb14b09b1c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22d24147_49ae6cc0",
        "filename": "common/charge_state_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1453,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-13T10:33:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason I put it here is that I thought if the update gets preempted by a request this way there is no race: either you read the old avg, or the new avg. The other way, you might get preempted while samples_recorded is already updated, while sample sum isn\u0027t yet.\nThis wouldn\u0027t be an issue after the first minute anymore.\nIs there another way to avoid this?",
      "parentUuid": "bcd4fc42_6b2a75d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1453,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1453,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "5ea59932af2618665d724c566dd6abfb14b09b1c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39664c8c_44af2ee3",
        "filename": "common/charge_state_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1453,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-13T17:45:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can add a mutex if you want to make this completely reliable. You may find that some cros_ec console commands are not completely reliable, there is a lower bar for correctness than host commands, which must function correctly in all circumstances to not break production.",
      "parentUuid": "22d24147_49ae6cc0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1453,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1453,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "5ea59932af2618665d724c566dd6abfb14b09b1c",
